From 9786c3a1ddbe0a7407e4b7057071c8bcccc1f905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lierfang Support Team <itsupport@lierfang.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:54:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ui/rdp: add the in-process RDP display backend on libvds

Add `-rdp`, an in-process RDP server built on libvds (ABI 2.0):

- ui/rdp-core.c: options, password/expiry, QMP/HMP `info rdp`,
  `encoder=openh264|vaapi` and `rendernode=`.
- ui/rdp-display.c: hands shareable guest framebuffers to libvds with
  vds_head_attach_shared() and reports damage with vds_head_damage();
  other surfaces keep the copy path. Buffers are released from a
  main-loop bottom half.
- ui/rdp-input.c: keyboard, pointer and wheel (clamped to 16 notches
  per event).
- ui/rdp-clipboard.c: text clipboard through the QEMU clipboard.
- audio/rdpaudio.c: `-audiodev rdp` playback backend (QOM type
  "audio-rdp", a mixing-engine backend).

Signed-off-by: Lierfang Support Team <itsupport@lierfang.com>
